# Day 2 - Project Structure and C++ Basics

## What I did today

- Checked the Unreal project folder structure
- Confirmed generated folders are ignored by Git
- Opened the Unreal C++ character class
- Learned the difference between .h and .cpp files
- Edited BeginPlay
- Printed the character name on screen
- Built and tested the project

## What I learned

- The .h file declares what a class has.
- The .cpp file defines what the class does.
- BeginPlay runs when the actor starts playing.
- Super::BeginPlay() should usually be called first.
- FString is Unreal's string type.
- GetName() returns the Unreal object name.

